@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
title HTTP Proxy and Test Utilities Architecture

package "Proxy Path" {
  component "HTTP Client" as Client
  component "HTTP Proxy" as Proxy <<Proxy>>
  component "Upstream Server" as Upstream <<Server>>

  Client --> Proxy : HTTP request\n(URI, headers, body)
  Proxy --> Upstream : Forward retained FullHttpRequest\n(after upstream channel active)
}

package "Test Utilities" {
  component "Test Client\n(Async HTTP Client,\nFixed Thread Pool)" as TestClient <<Client>>
  package "Test Server (Grizzly/Jersey)" as TestServer {
    component "Download Handler\nGET /download" as DownloadHandler
    component "Upload Handler" as UploadHandler
    component "Response API" as ResponseAPI
  }
}

folder "Local Filesystem" as FS

TestClient --> TestServer : HTTP requests
TestServer --> TestClient : Structured response {code,msg,data}
DownloadHandler --> FS : Check file exists\nread binary
DownloadHandler --> TestClient : application/octet-stream +\nContent-Disposition attachment\n(if file exists)\n(no attachment if not)
UploadHandler --> TestClient : Map payload {"filepath":<file name>}

TestServer --> DownloadHandler
TestServer --> UploadHandler
TestServer --> ResponseAPI

note right of Proxy
- Writes & flushes retained request only when upstream channel active
- No header/body transformation required during forwarding
- Debug logs may include current URI/headers/body
end note

note bottom of TestClient
- Counts successes where status code == 200
- Closes HTTP client and shuts down executor after run
- Example workload: 50 threads × 1000 GETs
end note

note bottom of DownloadHandler
Returns binary file when present; else no file entity
end note

@enduml